    native_link_rt_cuda_init_never_opens_libcuda_2026-11-22, P2, verified, "natively linked CUDA program: rt_cuda_init never opens libcuda (cuda-init-failed)", doc/08_tracking/bug/native_link_rt_cuda_init_never_opens_libcuda_2026-11-22.md, 1, doc/08_tracking/bug/native_link_rt_cuda_init_never_opens_libcuda_2026-11-22.md, 2026-11-22, 2026-11-26, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    native_link_rt_cuda_init_never_opens_libcuda_2026-11-22, 0, "2026-11-22 filed by work/cuda-compiler-bugs: processing_cuda_fill_probe linked with --runtime-path stage2-runtime-authority (rc 0, bin d23f4ff9137083ce) reports cuda-init-failed on a live GB10; strace shows no libcuda open, no libcuda string in binary. Provider env (SIMPLE_CUDA_PROVIDER_PATH) not tried. Runtime lane; related native_c_runtime_missing_cuda_provider_forwarders_2026-11-22."
    native_link_rt_cuda_init_never_opens_libcuda_2026-11-22, 1, "2026-11-26 work/bug-cuda-native-20261126 root cause: under --runtime-path <stage2-runtime-authority> the native-all archive's Rust rt_cuda_init owns the symbol. The link carries no runtime_dynload object, and native-all builds dynload REGISTRY_ONLY. The archive was built without feature cuda, so it returned NotInitialized=3 and never opened libcuda. Owner decision 2026-11-26: build the authority with cuda. Fix: native_all/Cargo.toml adds cuda to simple-runtime's features. It needs no SDK and the driver is dlopen'ed. Proof: the integ25 authority with only libsimple_native_all.a replaced by the cuda build from this source (cargo release -p simple-native-all); cuda_device_query_probe linked with --runtime-path. Results: init=0 count=1 name=NVIDIA GB10 capability=121; with SIMPLE_CUDA_LIB missing, init=303 and the clean sentinels, rc 0; readelf -d shows no NEEDED libcuda. Also fixed: the provider DSO was not dlopen-able because runtime_timestamp.c initial-exec TLS made it DF_STATIC_TLS. The next bootstrap-built authority must be re-proved."

